# Routes served by the application shell rather than their own prerendered
# file. Cloudflare Pages applies this file, and a 200 here is a rewrite, not
# a redirect: the address the reader shared stays in the address bar.
#
# The booking page carries the same title and description for every journey,
# so prerendering one file per journey wrote the same head thousands of
# times and pushed the deployment past the host's 20,000 file limit. Every
# route whose head is genuinely its own is still a real file, which is why
# only this one appears here.
/journey/*/booking  /index.html  200
